so far in 2022 streaming video accounted  for roughly half of the internet's  bandwidth with no signs of slowing down  this growth has not only strained  existing infrastructure but has also  challenged companies to expand the  presence of their content globally in  response companies have begun to look to  the public cloud to not only grow their  distribution infrastructure  but also expand it globally to serve  their viewers closer to where they are  solving for this has traditionally been  tricky for developers due to hurdles  such as complex configuration and  deployment this is why we introduced  media cdn a modern platform for  companies to efficiently scale and  deliver media content to anyone anywhere  on the globe all while providing a  seamless developer experience  let's take a closer look at media cdn by  walking through scenarios that an  imagined streaming service screening in  the cloud might face while trying to  build out their streaming service to  serve a global user base  screening in the cloud has a couple of  alpha customers in mind wendy and hanan  wendy is in sao paulo watching it on her  mobile phone and hanan is at home in  sydney on her fiber connection screening  in the cloud wants to serve their movies  to both of them in the highest possible  quality without excessive buffering or  choppiness  screening in the cloud cares about a few  key things that media cdn brings to the  table  the first is its global network that  allows them to serve their content as  close to wendy and hanan as possible  this is where media cdn shines because  its underlying infrastructure is  actually built on google's planet scale  network it's the same infrastructure  that supports youtube to serve videos to  users around the world  screening in the cloud gets to use this  network that spans more than 210  territories and 1300 cities screening in  the cloud can use this global network to  cache content from all of their origins  whether they're served via a google  cloud resource like a google cloud  storage bucket or reside in an origin  external to google cloud like within  hosts in their data centers that  predates their growth into the cloud as  screening in the cloud prepares to serve  their global user base with a production  ready service they'll be using another  set of features that sets media cdn  apart  those that ensure the delivery of their  content is secure this security spans  both secure content delivery and  policy-based restrictions that give  screening in the cloud granular control  on what is served where for securing  content delivery media cdn comes with  integrated ssl certificate management  there are no additional charges  associated with serving ssl traffic or  obtaining google managed certificates  after all protecting end user traffic  should not be at a premium  media cdn also adheres to the latest tls  support for better performance and  stronger encryption for their content  incorporating geo region and ip based  policies on their content  as far as controlling what content gets  delivered where screening in the cloud  can use cloud armor google's network  security service to apply allow and deny  list based rules  screening in the cloud for example may  have specific content that should not be  served to australia users as a whole  including hanan  to achieve this they can use gcloud to  create a security policy for media cdn  services and then attach a rule to that  policy that excludes users in australia  from accessing the specific content  they can then select the media cdn  service to which this policy applies and  attach it  with a few commands screening in the  cloud gets granular control over who can  access their content  security features are first class  citizens in the media cdn user  experience allowing for screening in the  cloud to be production ready  with origins set and security now  accounted for screening in the cloud can  begin to see the performance gains that  media cdn brings to the table with its  advanced caching  you see the global network that powers  media cdn is more than just google's  data centers rather it's google's data  centers points of presence and  integrations with isps that provide  multi-tiered caching functionality that  minimizes cache fill at each layer  ultimately this gives screening in the  cloud two key wins performance gains for  serving content close to the user and  origin shielding to reduce the load on  their own server's hosting content  finally screening in the cloud is eager  to deploy media cdn because it brought  an intuitive and well integrated  developer experience to their team this  experience spans the entire life cycle  of serving content from integrating with  the rest of their video delivery  pipeline to deploying the edge caches  for their content to monitoring and  logging these services in production in  the end screening in the cloud was able  to integrate media cdn with the rest of  their video delivery architecture  screening in the cloud first used the  transcoder api to translate the original  video file into multiple bit rates and  resolutions to provide appropriate  options for various device types and  network bandwidth of end users  the manifest file points to the various  video segments so that the end user's  video player can choose based on  availability bandwidth so that both  wendy and hanan can view the content  best suited for their internet  connectivity  given that with their global base comes  the potential for adding revenue streams  from advertising screening in the cloud  can add the video stitcher api to this  pipeline dynamically inserting ads into  their content before landing in its  origin fronted by media cdn screening in  the cloud also wants to make sure that  their service is not only performant but  reliable for all the users that come  after wendy and hanan  media cdn comes with integrated logging  and monitoring in cloud operations with  dashboards providing critical  information for their engineers  maintaining production  they can view information like cache  hits which display the quick performance  improvements that media cdn brings to  the table once enabled  they can also look at information like  blocked requests  which provide information that ensures  their security policies are working in  prod  and finally they can look at information  like response codes which can help them  quickly remediate issues that may affect  wendy and hanan's experience with the  content  to sum it up media cdn enabled screening  in the cloud too  utilize the same infrastructure that  powers youtube to serve rich content to  a global audience  achieve industry-leading offload rates  with deep caching infrastructure  reducing stress on origins  secure delivery of their content without  sacrificing performance  all while ensuring developers were able  to integrate this with the rest of their  video pipeline and their operations to  keep their services reliable  learn more by heading to  cloud.google.com  media cdn
 

